# Trivy suppressions for the release gate in .github/workflows/builder.yaml.
#
# The scan runs with `severity: HIGH,CRITICAL`, `ignore-unfixed: false` and
# `exit-code: 1`, so a single unfixable base-image CVE blocks the add-on image
# (all three architectures). This file is the deliberate escape hatch: it is
# empty on purpose, and every addition must be:
#
#   <CVE-id or package>  # <date> - <why it cannot be fixed> - <tracking issue>
#
# Example (do not enable without the justification above):
#   CVE-0000-00000  # 2026-01-01 - no upstream fix for the pinned base image - #123
#
# Prefer removing the offending package, or bumping the base image, over
# suppressing a finding.
